{"hits":{"hits":[{"created":"2006-04-11T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2023-03-07T01:16:54.847562+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/714255?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A714255"},"metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"08","artid":"059","year":2006,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1213103"},"page_start":"059","journal_title":"JHEP"}],"abstracts":[{"value":"We reconsider the calculation of a non-global QCD observable and find the possible breakdown of QCD coherence. This breakdown arises as a result of wide angle soft gluon emission developing a sensitivity to emission at small angles and it leads to the appearance of super-leading logarithms. We use the `gaps between jets' cross-section as a concrete example and illustrate that the new logarithms are intimately connected with the presence of Coulomb gluon contributions. We present some rough estimates of their potential phenomenological significance."}],"control_number":714255,"titles":[{"title":"Super-leading logarithms in non-global observables in QCD"},{"title":"QUANTUM CHROMODYNAMICS"},{"title":"SUPERLEADING"},{"title":"NONGLOBAL"},{"title":"Super-leading logarithms in non-global observables in QCD"}]},"id":"714255"}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Ahep-ph%2F0604094&size=10&page=1&fields=titles.title,abstracts.value,publication_info","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Ahep-ph%2F0604094&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxi